UNIT diff_hint
LANG js
PRIMARY-SHA256 2d15033b23e06a43fadec022b438345a002fa2db509fb185a9629ad23b37a777
SIG export function diff_hint(existing: string, profile: string): string
ABI text=string (UTF-16); the reconstruction exports a plain named function of two strings. The real diffHint takes two
  Buffers and decodes them as UTF-8; the seam passes text, so the reconstruction takes the strings directly.
MECHANISM R1 = String.prototype.split with the one-character separator "\n" (never a regex, never /\r?\n/). Line equality
  may compare whole strings (===). R4/R6 positions are code points: walk each line with Array.from or for-of (never [i],
  .length or .slice on the string, which count UTF-16 units and would move col and the 80-wide cut).
MECHANISM R7: JSON.stringify of the window, outer quotes removed, matches TABLE ESCAPE for the C0, quote and backslash rows
  (well-formed input: no lone surrogate reaches it); it does NOT escape INVISIBLE, which then needs its own pass over its
  output, and it must never see the two ELLIPSIS marks. A hand-written per-code-point map is equally correct.
PINNED regex INVISIBLE = /[\u000a-\u000d\u007f-\u00a0\u00ad\u034f\u0600-\u0605\u061c\u06dd\u070f\u0890\u0891\u08e2\u115f\u1160\u1680\u180b-\u180e\u2000-\u200f\u2028-\u202f\u205f-\u2064\u2066-\u206f\u2800\u3000\u3164\ufe00-\ufe0f\ufeff\uffa0\ufff9-\ufffb\u{110bd}\u{110cd}\u{13430}-\u{1343f}\u{1bca0}-\u{1bca3}\u{1d173}-\u{1d17a}\u{e0001}\u{e0020}-\u{e007f}\u{e0100}-\u{e01ef}]/gu CITED primary PINNED INVISIBLE — profile.mts line 78, the u flag
  (members above U+FFFF are whole code points); a match above U+FFFF becomes the braced form, any other the four-digit form
DEPENDS-ON none
PROVENANCE rederive@6199e2cc8b75 cli/lib/profile.mts diffHint (ts source, the js runtime); this file states the type
